# Applies to the repo-root build context, used by the two frontend images
# (frontend/web-app/Dockerfile and frontend/mobile-app/Dockerfile — see the
# comment at the top of each for why they need the root).
#
# The other three images build from their own subdirectory contexts and are
# governed by their own .dockerignore:
#   backend/api-gateway/.dockerignore
#   database/.dockerignore
#   ml-pipeline/fastapi-app/.dockerignore

.git
.github
.claude
.firebase

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.expo
**/.vite
**/.next
**/out

# Secrets — never bake these into an image layer.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
google-api-credentials.json
firebase-adminsdk.json

# Nothing outside frontend/ contributes to either frontend build. ml-pipeline
# alone is ~85 MB of model and feature data, so excluding these keeps the
# context small.
ml-pipeline
cloud_deployments
docs
database/migrations
database/seeds
database/scripts
database/backups
backend/api-gateway/src
backend/api-gateway/scripts

# Native project output from a local `expo prebuild` — regenerated, never an
# input, and large.
frontend/mobile-app/ios
frontend/mobile-app/android

# Test-only sources never reach the production bundle.
frontend/web-app/src/test
**/__tests__
**/*.test.js
**/*.test.jsx
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx

**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
RISK_REGISTER.md
